{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"iterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 50, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"optimalDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"threshold"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-4, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"barnesHutTheta"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = { _ in 1 }, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"using"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"generator"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SG","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RandomNumberGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every pair of vertices repels with force k²\/d and every edge attracts its ends with force"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" · d²\/k, where d is their distance (at least 0.01) and k is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optimalDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(default √(1\/n)). Each step moves every vertex along its net force by at most the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"temperature, which starts at a tenth of the larger side of the start’s bounding box (k\/10"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when every vertex starts at one point) and falls by the same amount each step, reaching 0"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" steps. Two vertices at exactly the same point repel as if 0.01"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart, along a direction fixed by their two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" offsets, so coincident vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separate deterministically. The run stops after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations"},{"type":"text","text":" steps, or earlier once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves’ root-sum-square divided by n is below "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"threshold"},{"type":"text","text":". Self-loops are ignored; parallel edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"add their weights. The drawing is in layout units (vertices end about k apart), not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rescaled. A directed graph is drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The start takes exactly 2n draws: x then y for each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, each the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"top 53 bits of one ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The same generator state gives the same drawing. Positions are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not stable across library versions, because the iteration is chaotic and any change in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"summation order changes its digits.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Repulsion is exact by default: O(n²) per step, for graphs up to a few thousand vertices.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"barnesHutTheta: θ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" approximates it with a Barnes–Hut quadtree, O(n log n) per step: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"square cell of side s whose centre of mass is at distance D from the vertex, and which does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not contain the vertex, acts as one body when s\/D < θ. θ = 1.2 suits graphs past about 5,000 vertices;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"θ = 0 is exact repulsion.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fruchterman and Reingold, “Graph drawing by force-directed placement”, Software: Practice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and Experience 21(11), 1991.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Barnes and Hut, “A hierarchical O(N log N) force-calculation algorithm”, Nature 324,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(iterations · (n² + m)) time exactly, O(iterations · (n log n + m)) with Barnes–Hut; O(n + m)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations ≥ 0"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optimalDistance"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is positive and finite;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"threshold ≥ 0"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"barnesHutTheta"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is finite and not negative; every weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is finite and not negative."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A force-directed drawing by Fruchterman and Reingold’s spring embedder, from positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawn uniformly in [0, 1)² from ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/FruchtermanReingoldLayout.swift#L42","fileName":"FruchtermanReingoldLayout.swift"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"t